-- title:
--   Discreteness and cocompactness of Γ₁ on the lattice tree
-- statement:
--   Write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and, for a valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, write $K_1$ for [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₁`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13), the topological closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at the valuation of $A_1$.
--
--   **Numerical data.** A nonzero squarefree $N$, primes $q$ and $q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, $q'\neq q$ and $5\le q$, $5\le q'$, and a nonzero $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$.
--
--   **The place above $q'$.** A valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q'$ a nonunit of $A_1$ (`hA₁`: `LiesOverPrime q'`), whose decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb Q$ preserves the valuation (`hiso₁`), together with a height-one prime $v_1$ of the integers of $\mathbb Q$ containing $q'$ (`hv₁`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_2,b_2$ with $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra precisely at the place $v$ dividing $q$ (`hdef₂`); a maximal order $\Lambda_2$ (an order contained in no strictly larger order) and an Eichler order $R_2$ of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in the first, with $R_2\le\Lambda_2$; a unit $n_2$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R₂ q'` (so $n_2$ lies in the finite-adelic box of $R_2$, so does $q'n_2^{-1}$, while $n_2^{-1}$ and $q'^{-1}n_2$ do not). Attached hypotheses: `hS₂`, that `meetOrder R₂ n₂` $=R_2\cap n_2R_2n_2^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq'$; `hnorm₂`, that conjugation by $n_2$ fixes this order; `hsq₂`, that right translation by $n_2$ on the class set of its finite-idele stabiliser is an involution; finiteness of the class sets of the stabilisers of `meetOrder R₂ n₂` and of $R_2$; and `hlaws₂` $=$ `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂`, namely that the edge Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the vertex Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the two degeneracy pushforwards intertwine edge and vertex Hecke operators at every prime other than $q$, and the joint kernel of the degeneracy pushforwards is stable under all edge Hecke operators.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side.** Rationals $a,b$ with $0<a$ or $0<b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the places dividing $q$ or $q'$ (`hB`), and a maximal order $\Lambda$ in it.
--
--   **Coarse moduli over $\mathbb Z[1/D]$ and the geometric fibre.** A field $Fbar$ which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and essentially of finite type over it; a scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Localization.Away (D : ℤ)`; a point $sbar$ of that base with values in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; an assignment $pt$ sending a fake elliptic curve for $(\Lambda,N)$ over a ring $S$ with a base point $s$ to a section of $\pi_X$ over $s$, subject to the four moduli axioms `pt_iso` (invariance under isomorphism), `pt_pullback` (compatibility with base change), `pt_surjective` and `pt_injective` (bijectivity on isomorphism classes over algebraically closed fields). A curve model $\mathfrak M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with function field $Fbar$, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ from $\mathfrak M.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $sbar$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he𝔐`), and a homomorphism $gal$ from $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to semilinear automorphisms of $Fbar$.
--
--   **The Hecke tower.** Tower data $\mathbb T$ of type `HeckeTower.TowerData q q' Fbar` (function fields $F(\ell)$ for primes $\ell\neq q,q'$, with integral, finite transition maps from $Fbar$), Galois actions $galT$ on each layer, involutions $W$ on $Fbar$ and $WT$ on the layers, and a witness $tw$ of type `ModuliTowerWitnessD Λ N q q' D Fbar X πX sbar pt 𝔐 e𝔐 gal 𝕋 galT W WT`, which interprets places of $Fbar$ and of the layers as fake elliptic curves with, respectively, extra $\ell$-level structure, compatibly with the Galois and Atkin–Lehner actions and with the degeneracy maps.
--
--   **Matrix realisation at $q'$.** An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_1$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ to $2\times 2$ matrices over $K_1$, the induced homomorphism $\rho_1$ to $\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_1)$ (`hρ₁`), a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi_1$ for $K_1$ inside the completion whose uniformiser maps to $q'$ (`hϖ₁`), and the assumption that `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₁ ρ₁` is a domain.
--
--   **Hecke elements and the groups $\Gamma_1$.** Families $s_1$ and $sf_1$, indexed by the primes $\ell\neq q,q'$, of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ and of its finite-adelic completion, with `hs₁`: for each $\ell$, the local component of $sf_1(\ell)$ is $s_1(\ell)\otimes 1$ away from $q'$ and is $1$ at the place above $q'$; the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_1(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₂ (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_1(\ell))=\ell$. A family $\Gamma_1$ of subgroups of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]^\times$ indexed by `HeckeTower.Obj q q'` $=$ `Option (AwayPrime q q')`, with `hΓ₁0`: $x\in\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ if and only if $x$ lies in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₂ v₁` — that is, at every height-one prime $w\neq v_1$ the image of $x$ in the local quaternion algebra lies in the subgroup generated by the units of the local box of $R_2$ — and the $q'$-adic valuation of $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$ is even; and `hΓ₁ℓ`: $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)=\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})\cap s_1(\ell)\,\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})\,s_1(\ell)^{-1}$.
--
--   **Normalising elements.** Families $w_1$ and $\bar w_1$ with `hw₁`: $w_1(\mathrm{none})$ lies in `awayUnits R₂ v₁` and has reduced norm $q'$, and for each $\ell$ the element $w_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ lies in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₂ (sf₁ ℓ)) v₁` and has reduced norm $q'$; and `hwbar₁` (clauses for $\mathrm{none}$ and for each $\ell$, summarised here): $\bar w_1$ has reduced norm $q$, is a unit of the relevant local box at all places $w\neq v_1$ not above $q$, and conjugation by it preserves the local boxes of $R_2$ (respectively of `meetOrder R₂ (sf₁ ℓ)`) and of $\Lambda_2$ at all places $w\neq v_1$.
--
--   **Local Galois data.** A homomorphism $dIso_1$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb Q$ to isometric automorphisms of the completion, inducing the given action (`hdIso₁`), and a character $\chi$ of that decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/2)$ which is trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on any Frobenius at $q'$ (`hχ₂`), and whose kernel consists exactly of the elements fixing all residue-field elements satisfying $x^{q'^2}=x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   **Coefficient rings.** A characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O_0$ with uniformiser $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with residue field of cardinality $q'$ and $(q')=(\pi)$, and with $K_1$ as its fraction field; an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $Onr$ which is a characteristic-zero domain, $\pi$-adically complete, with $(\pi)$ maximal, integral over $\mathcal O_0$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOa`), in which every monic polynomial of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOcl`), carrying an $\mathcal O_0$-automorphism $Fr$ with $Fr(x)\equiv x^{q'}\pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`); a homomorphism $vdet$ from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_1)$ to $\mathrm{Multiplicative}\,\mathbb Z$ measuring the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant (`hvdet`); and a ring map $\psi_0$ from $Onr$ to the completion together with the compatibilities `hπϖ` ($\pi\mapsto\varpi_1$), `hN₀` ($N$ invertible in $\mathcal O_0$), `h𝒪₀` (the image of $\mathcal O_0$ is the unit ball of $K_1$), `hψ₀` (the image of $\psi_0$ lies in the unit ball), `hψ₀𝒪` ($\psi_0$ extends the structure map of $\mathcal O_0$) and `hrk` (a rank-one condition on the valuation).
--
--   **Integral models and correspondences over $\mathcal O_0$.** A scheme $\mathcal X_0$ with a morphism $f_0$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ and a moduli assignment $pt_0$ making it a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves for $(\Lambda,N)$ in the sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (the four moduli axioms together with the universal property), with $\mathcal X_0$ integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell\neq q',q$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ with $g_0(\ell)$ and $ptT_0(\ell)$ satisfying `IsCoarseModuliT` for objects with extra $\ell$-level structure; two morphisms $d_{00}(\ell),d_{10}(\ell)\colon\mathcal Y_0(\ell)\to\mathcal X_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on moduli points forget the level structure (`hd₀`) and pass to the quotient by a level isogeny (`hd₁`); and endomorphisms $ar$, $\overline{ar}$ of $\mathcal X_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on moduli points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q'$ and at $q$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The uniformisation package.** Maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ which, for every $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, send a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum for $(\pi,K_1)$ over $B$ to a $B$-point of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$, over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$; and the hypothesis `hCD`, a conjunction of twelve clauses (summarised here): naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$ in $B$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of the matrices coming from `awayUnits R₂ v₁`, and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under that of the intersection of this group with its conjugate by $s_1(\ell)$; for algebraically closed $B$, surjectivity of $\Theta$ and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ at a fixed $Onr$-point together with the description of their fibres as orbits of those twisted actions; the corresponding universal properties of $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ among naturality- and invariance-satisfying families; compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_{00}(\ell)$ and, after the twisted action of $s_1(\ell)$, with $d_{10}(\ell)$; and compatibility of $\Theta$ with $ar$ via the Frobenius twist by $1$ and with $\overline{ar}$ via the twisted action of $\bar w_1(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let the vertices be the elements of [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪₀ K₁`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349), the homothety classes of full $\mathcal O_0$-lattices in $K_1^2$, with their $\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_1)$-action. The conclusion is the conjunction of four assertions:
--
--   (i) for every vertex $v$, the set of $g\in\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_1)$ which lie in the image $\rho_1(\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none}))$ and satisfy $g\cdot v=v$ is finite;
--
--   (ii) there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex $v$ admits some $g$ in $\rho_1(\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none}))$ with $g\cdot v\in S$;
--
--   (iii) for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\neq q'$ and $\ell\neq q$ and every vertex $v$, the set of $g\in\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_1)$ lying in the image under $\rho_1$ of $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$, the prime $\ell$ being read as an element of `AwayPrime q q'`, and satisfying $g\cdot v=v$ is finite;
--
--   (iv) for every such $\ell$ there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex $v$ admits some $g$ in that image with $g\cdot v\in S$.
--
--   Thus the image of $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$, and that of each $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$, acts on the lattice tree with finite stabilisers and with finitely many orbits on vertices.
--
--   This is the tree-theoretic discreteness and cocompactness input for the $q'$-side of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the even part of the group of units of the Eichler order which are integral away from the place above $q'$ acts on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over $K_1$ with finite vertex stabilisers and finitely many vertex orbits, and likewise for the congruence subgroups of the Hecke tower. It is used as a hypothesis for the statement producing a Mumford embedding from the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, where the quotient of the tree by such a group supplies the dual graph of the degenerate fibre.
